WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:01.390
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.625 --> 00:00:05.411
In this lesson, we cut long layers, with face-framing layers,

00:00:05.361 --> 00:00:08.350
while keeping almost all of the client's length.

00:00:08.753 --> 00:00:11.310
You heard the reason for each step in the theory lesson.

00:00:11.605 --> 00:00:12.670
Here, we do it.

00:00:13.189 --> 00:00:13.959
Step one:

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:14.919
preparation.

00:00:15.497 --> 00:00:16.519
Wash your hands.

00:00:16.626 --> 00:00:20.119
Scissors, combs and clips have been cleaned and disinfected.

00:00:20.547 --> 00:00:23.159
Wrap the neck strip, then fasten the cape over it.

00:00:23.812 --> 00:00:24.599
Step two:

00:00:24.768 --> 00:00:27.239
the consultation, while the hair is still dry.

00:00:27.578 --> 00:00:29.799
Look at the reference photo together with the client.

00:00:30.068 --> 00:00:31.319
Ask three things:

00:00:31.572 --> 00:00:35.419
how much to take off the ends, where the shortest layer at the front should start,

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:37.319
and whether she blow-dries every morning.

00:00:37.828 --> 00:00:41.959
Also ask how the last cut was done, and whether there was anything she didn't like.

00:00:42.216 --> 00:00:43.959
Agree using reference points:

00:00:44.138 --> 00:00:48.278
the ends here, the face-framing layers starting here, at the chin.

00:00:48.534 --> 00:00:50.599
Ask whether she often ties her hair up.

00:00:50.769 --> 00:00:53.718
Side layers that are too short will poke out of a ponytail.

00:00:54.142 --> 00:00:54.998
Read the hair:

00:00:55.264 --> 00:00:59.078
thick or fine, straight or curly, and where the whorls are.

00:00:59.264 --> 00:01:01.478
For fine hair, keep the layers few.

00:01:02.102 --> 00:01:02.846
Step three:

00:01:03.099 --> 00:01:06.686
shampoo, towel-dry, and detangle from the ends up.

00:01:07.185 --> 00:01:09.006
Part the hair the way the client will wear it.

00:01:09.376 --> 00:01:11.166
Here, it is a center parting.

00:01:11.413 --> 00:01:13.246
Section, and clip neatly.

00:01:13.595 --> 00:01:15.726
Keep the hair evenly damp throughout the cut.

00:01:16.439 --> 00:01:18.329
Step 4 the outer perimeter

00:01:18.999 --> 00:01:21.369
the client sits straight, head straight.

00:01:21.639 --> 00:01:24.889
Let the hair at the back down and comb it straight down the back

00:01:24.839 --> 00:01:26.489
at 0 degrees elevation.

00:01:27.159 --> 00:01:30.329
Hold the ends between two fingers at the agreed length.

00:01:30.759 --> 00:01:32.329
Keep your fingers horizontal.

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:35.369
Cut straight across just below your fingers.

00:01:35.799 --> 00:01:38.409
Cut the center first, then out to the sides.

00:01:38.839 --> 00:01:42.409
Look from behind. The perimeter is straight, parallel to the floor.

00:01:43.319 --> 00:01:47.129
Some clients like a slightly curved U shape or a pointed V shape.

00:01:47.399 --> 00:01:49.209
That must be agreed beforehand.

00:01:49.719 --> 00:01:53.129
Then continue to the sides, using the back line as the guide.

00:01:53.639 --> 00:01:55.609
This is the length of the whole haircut.

00:01:55.959 --> 00:01:58.729
The layers after this must not cut into it.

00:01:59.991 --> 00:02:00.853
Step five:

00:02:01.147 --> 00:02:02.693
long layers in the top.

00:02:02.868 --> 00:02:06.853
Section off the top, from the corners of the forehead back to the crown.

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:10.636
Comb the whole top section straight up, to 180°,

00:02:10.586 --> 00:02:14.613
gathered to a single point right above the top of the head.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.013
That is a stationary guideline.

00:02:17.417 --> 00:02:20.373
Hold it between two fingers, and cut straight across.

00:02:20.722 --> 00:02:22.933
The lower you cut, the shorter the layers.

00:02:23.177 --> 00:02:27.093
The first time, cut only a little, then let the hair down to look.

00:02:27.189 --> 00:02:28.373
You can always go shorter.

00:02:29.028 --> 00:02:30.867
Let the hair down, and look:

00:02:31.267 --> 00:02:34.778
the hair on top is the shortest, getting longer further down,

00:02:34.728 --> 00:02:36.707
and connecting into the perimeter.

00:02:37.119 --> 00:02:41.347
If you want the layers more visible, cut a little more, exactly the same way.

00:02:41.846 --> 00:02:45.507
Do not cut the layers on top too short, especially at the whorl.

00:02:45.767 --> 00:02:47.267
The hair will stand straight up.

00:02:47.924 --> 00:02:48.879
Step six:

00:02:49.136 --> 00:02:51.279
the sides, keeping length at the front.

00:02:51.713 --> 00:02:55.886
Start with a vertical section just behind the ear, lifted away from the head,

00:02:55.836 --> 00:02:57.599
connecting to the layers on top.

00:02:58.101 --> 00:03:00.079
This section is a stationary guideline.

00:03:00.512 --> 00:03:04.634
Then take a vertical section in front of the ear, and over-direct it back,

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:06.559
to exactly where that guideline is.

00:03:06.987 --> 00:03:09.679
Cut only the ends that extend past your fingers.

00:03:09.861 --> 00:03:12.879
The hair at the front will be longer, and won't lose length.

00:03:13.193 --> 00:03:16.570
Do exactly the same on the other side, with the same guideline,

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:17.679
and the same tension.

00:03:18.349 --> 00:03:19.132
Step seven:

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:20.892
the face-framing layers.

00:03:21.277 --> 00:03:23.232
Take a triangular section at the front,

00:03:23.182 --> 00:03:25.772
from the parting down to the corner of the forehead.

00:03:26.243 --> 00:03:28.412
Comb it forward, in front of the face.

00:03:28.917 --> 00:03:30.812
Ask the client to close her eyes.

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:36.283
Hold the section between two fingers, on a diagonal, with the top end at the chin,

00:03:36.233 --> 00:03:38.012
exactly at the agreed point.

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:42.492
Cut along that diagonal, with the scissor tips pointing away from her face.

00:03:42.741 --> 00:03:46.408
The next section, behind the first, is also combed forward,

00:03:46.358 --> 00:03:48.492
to exactly where the first one is,

00:03:48.681 --> 00:03:49.692
and cut to match it.

00:03:50.199 --> 00:03:55.559
Because it is over-directed forward, the hair further back gets gradually longer,

00:03:55.509 --> 00:03:57.132
softly framing the face.

00:03:57.641 --> 00:04:01.052
Then do the other side, at exactly the same height as this side.

00:04:01.763 --> 00:04:02.581
Step eight:

00:04:02.824 --> 00:04:03.701
cross-check.

00:04:04.022 --> 00:04:07.941
Wherever you cut with vertical sections, check with horizontal sections.

00:04:08.204 --> 00:04:10.021
Anything that sticks out, trim it.

00:04:10.529 --> 00:04:13.141
Then stand behind the client, and look in the mirror.

00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:16.644
Pull the two shortest pieces on each side of the face down,

00:04:16.594 --> 00:04:17.941
and compare their height.

00:04:18.369 --> 00:04:21.941
If they are uneven, trim the longer side, a little at a time.

00:04:22.515 --> 00:04:23.380
Step nine:

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:24.260
blow-dry.

00:04:24.796 --> 00:04:26.676
Dry in the direction of the hair,

00:04:26.626 --> 00:04:29.780
using a round brush to lift the roots gently at the top,

00:04:30.097 --> 00:04:33.460
and to roll the face-framing layers gently away from the face.

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:35.460
Once dry, look again:

00:04:35.887 --> 00:04:40.340
are both sides balanced, is the volume even, are the ends still thick?

00:04:40.845 --> 00:04:44.100
Wherever it is uneven, trim lightly while the hair is dry.

00:04:44.444 --> 00:04:47.096
Long layers also look good left to dry naturally,

00:04:47.046 --> 00:04:49.220
as long as the layers are not too short.

00:04:49.618 --> 00:04:51.060
Show the client both ways:

00:04:51.238 --> 00:04:53.460
blow-drying, and letting it dry naturally.

00:04:54.064 --> 00:04:56.594
A few things to keep in mind throughout a layered cut.

00:04:56.933 --> 00:04:58.994
First, stand in the right place.

00:04:59.278 --> 00:05:00.425
Move around the client,

00:05:00.375 --> 00:05:03.714
so your body is always right in front of the section you are cutting.

00:05:04.141 --> 00:05:08.194
Stand off to the side, and your hands drift with you, without you noticing.

00:05:08.722 --> 00:05:10.674
Next, keep the elevation.

00:05:11.102 --> 00:05:15.474
As the cut goes on and your arms get tired, your hands slowly drop.

00:05:15.732 --> 00:05:18.434
Change the elevation, and the layers change too.

00:05:18.688 --> 00:05:20.034
And always start long.

00:05:20.223 --> 00:05:21.314
You can always trim more.

00:05:21.983 --> 00:05:22.767
Step ten:

00:05:22.944 --> 00:05:23.647
the finish.

00:05:24.097 --> 00:05:25.487
Brush off the loose hair.

00:05:25.668 --> 00:05:27.765
Show the client the back with a hand mirror,

00:05:27.715 --> 00:05:30.046
and ask whether she would like anything adjusted.

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:33.487
Show her how to blow-dry the face-framing layers at home.

00:05:33.836 --> 00:05:35.247
Write it in the client record:

00:05:35.455 --> 00:05:37.487
the length, and where the layers start.

00:05:37.977 --> 00:05:42.527
With long layers, many clients come back for a trim after about two or three months.

00:05:42.616 --> 00:05:46.767
Regular trims keep the ends thick, and the layers hold their shape longer.

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:48.776
After the client leaves:

00:05:48.879 --> 00:05:52.331
scissors, combs and clips are cleaned and disinfected,

00:05:52.281 --> 00:05:54.536
as in the lesson on cleaning tools.

00:05:54.879 --> 00:05:57.896
Throw away the neck strip, and sweep up the hair under the chair.

00:05:58.239 --> 00:06:01.176
And now, please take the short quiz below the video.
